{
  "mn107:0.1": "Middle Discourses 107 ",
  "mn107:0.2": "With Moggallāna the Accountant ",
  "mn107:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn107:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in the stilt longhouse of Migāra’s mother in the Eastern Monastery. ",
  "mn107:1.3": "Then the brahmin Moggallāna the Accountant went up to the Buddha, and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn107:1.4": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to the Buddha: ",
  "mn107:2.1": "“Worthy Gotama, in this stilt longhouse we can see gradual training, gradual progress, and gradual practice ",
  "mn107:2.2": "down to the last step of the staircase. ",
  "mn107:2.3": "Among the brahmins we can see gradual training, gradual progress, and gradual practice ",
  "mn107:2.4": "in recitation. ",
  "mn107:2.5": "Among archers we can see gradual training, gradual progress, and gradual practice ",
  "mn107:2.6": "in archery. ",
  "mn107:2.7": "Among us accountants, who earn a living by accounting, we can see gradual training, gradual progress, and gradual practice ",
  "mn107:2.8": "in mathematics. ",
  "mn107:2.9": "For when we get an apprentice we first make them count: ",
  "mn107:2.10": "‘One one, two twos, three threes, four fours, five fives, six sixes, seven sevens, eight eights, nine nines, ten tens.’ ",
  "mn107:2.11": "We even make them count up to a hundred. ",
  "mn107:2.12": "Is it possible to similarly describe a gradual training, gradual progress, and gradual pra